=== P6: the SECOND variable -- the upstream CLOCK, on a clean instrument
    Three confounds had to die first, and each reversed or inflated the answer:
      (a) seeding stage 1 as a delta at its rail: the slow cells had not SPREAD yet,
          which reads as a clock effect and reversed the sign of the trend;
      (b) measuring P(s2 low, s1 high): conditioning on stage 1 surviving excludes
          exactly the trajectories that dipped, and the exclusion grows with speed;
      (c) pre-equilibrating the joint chain: stage 2 AGES during it -- at speed 1/8
          it had already accumulated 14.6% error before the window opened.
    Clean instrument: stage 1 REFLECTED at its saddle (it can never escape, so
    nothing is conditioned), seeded from its EXACT stationary law (speed-independent,
    since scaling every rate equally leaves it unchanged), stage 2 fresh at its rail.
   speed    P(s2 low)   penalty   limit it approaches
   0.125  1.54691e-02     4.244                frozen
   0.250  1.56480e-02     4.293                frozen
   0.500  1.59816e-02     4.385                frozen
   1.000  1.61900e-02     4.442                frozen
   2.000  1.51458e-02     4.155                frozen
   4.000  1.20339e-02     3.302                frozen
   8.000  8.58730e-03     2.356              fast-avg
  16.000  6.68879e-03     1.835              fast-avg
  32.000  5.99657e-03     1.645              fast-avg
  FROZEN-upstream formula <exp(-dA*Om)>   = 4.845;  slow plateau measures 4.244..4.442
  FAST-averaging formula  exp(-<dA>*Om)   = 1.139;  fast tail measures 1.645 and still falling
  -> P6 HOLDS: the penalty interpolates between the two limits as the upstream clock varies. The frozen formula is the SLOW limit (not the fast one), and the fall toward the mean-landscape rate as the upstream speeds up is MOTIONAL NARROWING
  -> so §91's margin law is a FROZEN-upstream statement. All of §91's variants ran
     at speed 1, inside the plateau, which is why one variable sufficed there.

